# Sidebar & navigation: single source of truth

## Rule

- **All app sidebar/navigation structure comes from one place:** `src/lib/nav/navFactory.ts`.
- **Desktop** (`app-sidebar-nav.tsx`) and **mobile** (`mobile-sidebar.tsx`) both consume it via `getNavSectionsForShell()` in `src/lib/nav/shellNav.ts`.
- **Do not** add or edit nav item arrays (hrefs, labels, icons) inside `mobile-sidebar.tsx` or `app-sidebar-nav.tsx`. Those components only render data from the nav factory.

## When adding or changing a sidebar item

1. **Edit only:** `src/lib/nav/navFactory.ts`
   - Add or change the item in the correct section builder: `buildExecutiveSection`, `buildSalesSection`, `buildLaunchSection`, `buildOperationsSection`, `buildSystemSection`, or `buildFranchisorSections`.
   - Use an existing `AppTranslationKey` for the label, or add a new one (step 2).
2. **If the label is new:** add the key and strings in `src/lib/app-translations.ts` (e.g. `navMyNewPage: 'My New Page'` in EN and ES).
3. **Optional:** If the item should show an alert badge (e.g. handoffs, open issues, missed tasks), add `alertKey` to the item in `navFactory.ts` and ensure that key exists in `NavAlertCounts` in `src/actions/nav-alerts.ts`.

## File roles

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/lib/nav/navFactory.ts` | **Only place** that defines sections and items (href, labelKey, icon, alertKey). |
| `src/lib/nav/shellNav.ts` | Maps shell (owner_operator / franchisee / franchisor) to org type and calls `buildNavSections`. |
| `src/components/app/app-sidebar-nav.tsx` | Renders sections from `getNavSectionsForShell()`; do not add items here. |
| `src/components/app/mobile-sidebar.tsx` | Renders same sections from `getNavSectionsForShell()` with mobile layout; do not add items here. |
| `src/lib/app-translations.ts` | Add new `nav*` keys here when you add new items in navFactory. |

## Checklist before shipping sidebar changes

- [ ] Change made in `navFactory.ts` only (no duplicate arrays in mobile or desktop components).
- [ ] New labels added to `app-translations.ts` if needed.
- [ ] Both desktop and mobile sidebars will pick up the change automatically (no extra edits in `mobile-sidebar.tsx` or `app-sidebar-nav.tsx` for the new link).
